DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:Easy Indoor Spin (45 min)
DESCRIPTION:Maintain aerobic circulation and keep legs moving with minimal fatigue.\n45 min smooth indoor trainer ride in Zone 1-2\, maintaining high cadence (90-100 RPM).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cyclist-taper-20260916@aitrainingplan
DTSTAMP:20260916T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Taper Openers (60 min)
DESCRIPTION:Touch on race intensity to maintain neuromuscular sharpness without building fatigue.\n15 min easy warm-up\, 4 x 3 min at threshold effort with 3 min easy spin recovery\, 21 min easy cool-down.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cyclist-taper-20260917@aitrainingplan
DTSTAMP:20260917T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260917
SUMMARY:Recovery Indoor Ride (45 min)
DESCRIPTION:Flush residual fatigue from Wednesday's openers.\n45 min easy indoor spin strictly in Zone 1.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cyclist-taper-20260919@aitrainingplan
DTSTAMP:20260919T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260919
SUMMARY:Outdoor Taper Long Ride (90 min)
DESCRIPTION:Practice Gran Fondo pacing and climbing position without draining energy stores.\n20 min easy warm-up\, 50 min moderate tempo ride on rolling hills with short steady climb efforts\, 20 min easy cool-down.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cyclist-taper-20260920@aitrainingplan
DTSTAMP:20260920T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260920
SUMMARY:Outdoor Easy Spin (45 min)
DESCRIPTION:Promote active recovery and check gear for race week.\n45 min easy outdoor spin on flat terrain in Zone 1.
END:VEVENT
